frida (16.4.0~pirogue1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Strip auto/ prefix for debian/* tags.
  * Fix missing build-dep: python3-setuptools.
  * Remove extraneous build-dep: curl.
  * Fix missing --recursive option for `git submodule` operations.
  * Make sure to install frida-core-1.0.{deps,vapi} in
    /usr/share/vala/vapi/ as before: upstream build system modifications
    lead to their being installed under a directory matching the build
    directory (e.g. /home/kibi/deb-frida). Since modifying the build
    system doesn't seem easy, move them into place after installation.
  * Adjust frida-core-1.0.pc accordingly. It doesn't seem to be usable
    anyway because it references a number of libraries only available via
    the SDK/toolchain downloaded at the beginning of the build, but it
    makes sense to avoid adding new problems.
  * New upstream release.

 -- Cyril Brulebois <cyril@debamax.com>  Fri, 09 Aug 2024 16:18:14 +0200

